  "id": "two-stage-sampling",
  "term": "two-stage sampling",
  "definition": "Two-stage sampling is a sampling method in which researchers first randomly choose groups or clusters from a larger set, then randomly select individual elements from within each chosen group. In the source packet, the groups are first-stage units and the selected elements within them are second-stage units.",
